77 focused tests passed; scratch suite of 7 tests passed, including independent old-generation completion, held persistence and notifier-first ordering cases.
Independent baseline run reproduced the expected three failures; its generation-separation case passed as before.
Post-repository boundary probe: a deliberately delayed custom refresh callback allows a later repository refresh to finish before the interceptor receives an older result; its legacy access-token write then restores the older access token. This fails identically on baseline and current head. The custom callback delay is absent from the stock provider wiring; not a regression introduced by this change. Separate raw logs /tmp/1185-boundary-current.log and /tmp/1185-boundary-baseline.log preserve the probe.
